{"id":"diagram-revision-fa2cea67-c65d-4167-b6f4-b9b461ed3640","diagramId":"diagram-09297952-73c4-4e76-9f93-1c3a67a79b76","parentId":"diagram-revision-8c400f67-871e-4388-acb1-c9b562aeb278","diagram":{"id":"alt-company","revision":1,"diagramId":"diagram-09297952-73c4-4e76-9f93-1c3a67a79b76","revisionId":"diagram-revision-fa2cea67-c65d-4167-b6f4-b9b461ed3640","content":{"revisionId":"alt-company:1","ascii":"SHOPIFY COMPANY MAP | FY2018-Q3 2026 | G1-G3, evidence at G6\n|\n+-- [S] Thesis: make commerce better for everyone\n|   +-- [S] Merchant success drives Shopify's success\n|   +-- Merchant GMV -[D:mech]-> merchant solutions revenue\n|   |   +-- [R] FY25: $8.804B of $11.556B revenue, or 76.2%\n|   +-- [I] Superior outcomes lack a matched off-platform comparison\n|\n+-- Value engine: management's changing flywheel language\n|   +-- [S] 2019: lower barriers, more merchants, tools, success\n|   +-- [S] Q4 2025: Shop discovery, intent, trust, conversion, return\n|   +-- [S] Q1 2026: commerce intelligence plus demand conversion\n|   +-- [I] Feedback loops lack measured causal validation\n|\n+-- Scale and monetization\n|   +-- [R] GMV: $41B FY18 -> $378.4B FY25; FY18 is seed-only\n|   +-- [R] Revenue: $1.07B FY18 -> $11.556B FY25; FY18 seed-only\n|   +-- [R] Payments penetration: 40.4% FY18 -> 65.6% FY25\n|   +-- [R] FY25 merchant solutions revenue / GMV: 2.33%\n|   +-- [I] Seed's net-take and FCF attribution lack full inputs here\n|\n+-- Eight strategic domains: analytical map\n|   +-- Payments and merchant finance: monetize merchant volume\n|   |   +-- [R] FY25 Payments processed $248.1B of GMV\n|   +-- Buyer network: Shop Pay and Shop connect buyers to merchants\n|   |   +-- [S] Q3 2026 Shop GMV more than doubled year-on-year\n|   +-- Merchant on-ramps and range: first sale through enterprise\n|   |   +-- [R] FY21: approximately 2,063,000 merchants; later \"millions\"\n|   +-- Selling surfaces: online, POS, B2B, partner channels\n|   |   +-- [S] FY25 offline revenue $748M; B2B GMV grew 96%\n|   +-- Global reach: localization and product availability\n|   |   +-- [S] FY25 international revenue grew 36%\n|   +-- Shipping and fulfillment: build, then partner\n|   |   +-- [R] FY23 logistics-sale impairment: $1.340B\n|   +-- Platform and ecosystem: extensible commerce software\n|   |   +-- [R] FY25 App Store: more than 21,000 apps\n|   +-- Commerce intelligence: shared data, merchant tools, discovery\n|       +-- [S] Q1 2026: intelligence feeds tools and merchant success\n|\n+-- Cross-domain dependencies retain their original grades\n|   +-- Payments -[D:mech]-> on-Shopify Shop Pay; seed product gate\n|   +-- Shop Pay -[D:claim]-> more merchants adopt Payments\n|   +-- Payments availability -[D:assoc]-> international take rate\n|   +-- Catalog + Shop Pay -[D:data]-> agentic channels; seed linkage\n|   +-- [I] Product gates and feedback claims need separate evidence\n|\n+-- Time axis: six analytical eras, not reported segments\n|   +-- Expand -> Surge -> Build-ahead -> Reckoning\n|   +-- Focused compounding -> Reacceleration\n|   +-- [I] Logistics exit is an adaptation; later growth is not proof\n|\n+-- Evidence discipline\n    +-- [I] Seed audit: 112 claims; underlying claim ledger not supplied\n    +-- [I] No measured causal link established in these excerpts\n    +-- [R] Filing / arithmetic | [S] management statement\n    +-- [I] inference | [X] contradicted claim\n    +-- D = dependency; C = sequence; M = structure; O = control\n    +-- Grades: mech | causal | assoc | data | claim | untestable | contra\n\nNAVIGATION | Linked labels open subject canvases.\nDirect: Payments; Merchant on-ramps; Global reach; Platform;\n        Commerce intelligence; Time axis (Allocation and capital).\nSelling surfaces: via Merchant on-ramps > PHYSICAL RETAIL.\nShipping and fulfillment: via Time axis > logistics sold.\nBuyer Network (Shopify 04): unavailable; text only, no jump.\nNavigation is not a causal or evidential relationship.","asciiSha256":"a50